      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(tui): keep skill approvals in the terminal",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWorkspace skill changes initiated from the TUI currently forward plugin approval requests to configured messaging channels. The initiating terminal stays blocked while Telegram receives a generic security-style approval message with little workspace-skill context.\n\nCloses #100250.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Route pending plugin approvals into the TUI session that initiated the tool call.\n- Present the plugin, tool, severity, requested action, and allowed decisions in a terminal modal.\n- Support both Gateway-backed TUI sessions and embedded `tui --local` through a process-local approval broker.\n- Bind Gateway approval review to the authenticated internal TUI device instead of widening approval visibility.\n- Suppress messaging-channel fallback only for plugin approvals; configured exec-approval forwarding remains unchanged.\n- Refresh pending approvals after event gaps/reconnects and keep nested overlay focus ownership deterministic.\n- Sanitize terminal control, newline, and bidi text before rendering approval content.\n\n## User Impact\n\nTUI users can review and resolve workspace skill changes without switching to Telegram. Telegram no longer receives these terminal-local plugin approval requests. Denial, timeout, reconnect, and embedded-local behavior remain fail-closed.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Rebased onto `origin/main` at `9c5ea29e384d36ff3439c551cd0314542d4862f1`.\n- `git diff --check`\n- `oxfmt --check` for all 30 changed files\n- Focused local Vitest: 365 tests passed across 6 shards\n- Local PTY harness: 16 tests passed\n- Crabbox/Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kwrr5zsgrysrr1q5hathmbfz` (`swift-lobster`)\n  - `check:changed`: core/core-test typechecks, core/UI/packages lint, import-cycle and policy guards passed\n  - Remote PTY plus `tui --local`: 20 tests passed\n  - Actions hydration run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28735592088\n- Fresh exact-head autoreview: no actionable findings; patch correct at 0.82 confidence\n",
